entries.definition_en:
δημόσιος, -α, -ον
 (δῆμος), [in LXX: 2Ma.6:10, 3Ma.2:27 4:7 * ;] 
belonging to the people, public: Act.5:18; dative fem. used adverbially (cl.); 
 __(a) at the public expense, by public consent; 
 __(b) publicly: Act.16:37 18:28 20:20.†
 (AS)

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.23.29; 
 son of: Baanah (H1196H); also called Heldai at 1Ch.27.15; Heled at 1Ch.11.30; 
 § Heleb = "milk"
 son of Baanah, the Netophathite, and one of David's mighty warriors; also spelled 'Heled' ( che.led (חֵ֫לֶד "Heled" H2466))

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.42a; 
 son of: Caleb (H3612H); 
 brother of: Hur (H2354), Jesher (H3475), Shobab (H7727H), Ardon (H0715), Haran (H2771B), Moza (H4162), Gazez (H1495), Jahdai (H3056), Sheber (H7669), Tirhanah (H8647), Shaaph (H8174H), Sheva (H7724) and Achsah (H5915H); 
 father of: Ziph (H2128I) and Hebron (H2275I) 
 § Mesha = "deliverance"
 the eldest son of Caleb by his wife Azubah and grandson of Hezron

A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Gen.4.26; 
 son of: Seth (H8352); 
 father of: Kenan (H7018); also called Enos at Luk.3.38; 
Also named: Enōs (Ἐνώς "Enos" G1800) 
 § Enos = "man"
 son of Seth

A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.44; 
 son of: Abdi (H5660); 
 father of: Jeduthun (H3038); also called Kushaiah at 1Ch.15.17; 
Another name of qi.shi (קִישִׁי "Kishi" H7029) 
 § Kushaiah = "bow of Jehovah"
1) father of Ethan the Merarite
1a) same as 'Kish' or 'Kishi'
